  "formal": {
    "project": "research/semaev_reassociation_audit_20261113/lean",
    "theorem": "SemaevReassociationAudit.actual_source_order_reassociation_with_control",
    "statement": "theorem actual_source_order_reassociation_with_control : (∀ (R : Type) [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] (D : ℕ) (p : Polynomial R), p.natDegree ≤ D → ∀ W : WeierstrassCurve R, doubleStep D p W.b₂ W.b₄ W.b₆ W.b₈ = sourceBalanced D p W) ∧ (∀ (K : Type) [Field K] (W : WeierstrassCurve.Affine K) (n : ℕ), recursivePolynomial W (n+2) = sourceBalanced (2^(n+1)) (recursivePolynomial W n) (W.map (coefficientEmbedding n))) ∧ s4Ring (0 : ℚ) 0 0 1 0 1 2 3 ≠ s4Ring (0 : ℚ) 0 0 1 0 2 1 3",
    "decl_sha256": "bf6fbf6ca38648e090bba826e2ba9a2e8054563448ff16b560d7d96489293e1b",
    "scope": "Actual general-Weierstrass S3 two-step fixed-size resultant reassociation into the existing source-ordered S4 block over every commutative integral domain, for every declared old sizeD>=natDegreeP, including zero P, repeated coordinates and every characteristic. Actual bivariate source/symmetry/degree, specialization and generic leading-coefficient proof, generic evaluation homomorphism proved identity on the three-variable polynomial ring, literal doubleStep and actual recursivePolynomial W(n+2) equality to sourceBalanced at every canonical stage. Actual Weierstrass-curve S4 cross-pair symmetry and rotation give exact source argument order. Direct rational independent-b coefficient control refutes unrestricted S4 cross symmetry; no qualified source refutation. This normalizes the k=2 S4-block split at every arity>=5, not all arbitrary k>=3, full higher permutation invariance or absolute irreducibility. No new native experiment or execution assurance.",
